Now let me find where `createUniversalClassSchedule` is called and check if it's being called multiple times accidentally.

OK, so the 409 is from `EnrollmentService::store` when the student already has an active course with the same subject. The error code is `duplicate_active_course`.

But in `universalSchedulerApi.js`, it already handles this:
```js
if (res.status === 409 && body?.code === 'duplicate_active_course') {
  const err = new Error(body.message || '該學生已有相同科目的進行中課程');
  err.isDuplicateCourse = true;
  err.conflicts = body.conflicts || [];
  err.originalPayload = normalizedPayload;
  throw err;
}
```

So the API is catching the conflict and throwing an error with metadata attached. Now I need to trace back where `createUniversalClassSchedule` is being invoked and figure out why it's being called multiple times instead of just once.

